1
00:05:24,829 --> 00:05:28,040
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

2
00:05:28,874 --> 00:05:31,544
It's all right. I'm not gonna hurt you.

3
00:05:31,836 --> 00:05:32,962
What do you want?

4
00:05:33,088 --> 00:05:33,922
I thought you were...

5
00:05:34,047 --> 00:05:35,090
What?

6
00:05:36,049 --> 00:05:37,425
I don't know.

7
00:05:49,145 --> 00:05:51,815
Help! Help!

8
00:05:55,235 --> 00:05:57,362
Help! Help!

9
00:06:01,116 --> 00:06:02,200
Stop!

10
00:06:08,414 --> 00:06:12,460
- What? What?
- It's okay. Come here.

11
00:06:32,730 --> 00:06:35,733
It's okay. Calm down.
Everything's gonna be fine.

12
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,067
What was in there?

13
00:06:37,277 --> 00:06:39,195
Just gimme a minute
to figure things out.

14
00:06:39,279 --> 00:06:42,282
- Why were you afraid of that room?
- Gimme a minute I said.

15
00:06:47,953 --> 00:06:50,080
How many people are in this thing?

16
00:06:52,542 --> 00:06:55,503
Listen. We can't go
climbing around in here.

17
00:06:55,753 --> 00:06:56,879
Why not?

18
00:06:58,798 --> 00:07:01,342
- There are traps.
- What do you mean traps?

19
00:07:01,467 --> 00:07:04,637
Booby traps. I looked
into a room down there and

20
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,472
something almost cut my head off.

21
00:07:10,851 --> 00:07:15,355
Holy cats. Holy, holy cats.

22
00:07:34,625 --> 00:07:37,462
You alright? Mister?

23
00:07:40,215 --> 00:07:41,215
Worth!

24
00:07:46,346 --> 00:07:47,346
Don't worry.

25
00:07:53,478 --> 00:07:54,478
I hit my head.

26
00:07:54,729 --> 00:07:59,317
Let me take a look at that.
I'm a doctor. It doesn't look that bad.

27
00:08:03,363 --> 00:08:04,906
What the hell are you doing?

28
00:08:18,294 --> 00:08:20,922
Hey, old man,
did you hear what I said?

29
00:08:41,776 --> 00:08:45,905
Motion detectors. Integrated
into the walls. Tough to spot.

30
00:08:47,615 --> 00:08:50,701
Oh god, oh god, oh god.

31
00:08:54,164 --> 00:08:57,500
Wait a second.
Let's all just relax for a minute.

32
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:01,712
Does anybody remember
how they got here?

33
00:09:09,887 --> 00:09:10,930
Perogies.

34
00:09:14,809 --> 00:09:16,018
I was eating dinner.

35
00:09:16,561 --> 00:09:17,853
Perogies. Cheese and potatoes.

36
00:09:17,937 --> 00:09:20,606
I ran out of sour cream and then
I went to the fridge and then...

37
00:09:21,691 --> 00:09:22,691
I don't know.

38
00:09:23,734 --> 00:09:26,446
You? Leaven?

39
00:09:28,155 --> 00:09:31,616
I, I just went to bed and...

40
00:09:34,495 --> 00:09:35,496
What about you?

41
00:09:37,707 --> 00:09:39,250
I just woke up here.

42
00:09:39,584 --> 00:09:40,710
Middle of the night.

43
00:09:41,544 --> 00:09:44,046
It's like Chile. They always come
in the middle of the night.

44
00:09:45,172 --> 00:09:46,006
Who?

45
00:09:46,131 --> 00:09:48,676
Only the goverment could build
something this ugly.

46
00:09:48,801 --> 00:09:49,885
It ain't government.

47
00:09:50,010 --> 00:09:52,346
- Then what is it?
- I don't know.

48
00:09:53,764 --> 00:09:54,974
Aliens.

49
00:09:59,604 --> 00:10:01,814
Please.
We're spooked enough as it is.

50
00:10:01,897 --> 00:10:06,611
Let's rule out aliens for now and
concentrate on what we know.

51
00:10:06,694 --> 00:10:07,862
My mom's gonna freak.

52
00:10:08,654 --> 00:10:09,654
Rennes?

53
00:10:10,365 --> 00:10:14,035
- I just won't be there. They'll freak.
- What do you think, Rennes?

54
00:10:14,869 --> 00:10:17,246
We won't solve jack shit sittin' still.

55
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:19,790
I'm moving in a straight line
'till I get to the end.

56
00:10:20,416 --> 00:10:21,960
All right, I tend to agree.

57
00:10:22,335 --> 00:10:24,712
- Shouldn't we wait here?
- For what?

58
00:10:25,129 --> 00:10:26,630
To see if anybody comes.

59
00:10:26,922 --> 00:10:28,173
No one is gonna come.

60
00:10:28,341 --> 00:10:32,178
Look. There is a way in here,
so there's gotta be a way out.

61
00:10:32,762 --> 00:10:34,847
We can avoid
the traps using the boot.

62
00:10:35,390 --> 00:10:38,851
Holloway is it?
What do you think? Look for an exit?

63
00:10:39,602 --> 00:10:40,602
Okay.

64
00:10:41,479 --> 00:10:42,605
What about you?

65
00:10:42,855 --> 00:10:46,191
- It can't be that simple.
- It won't be that simple.

66
00:10:46,901 --> 00:10:50,320
Look around.
Take a good long looksee.

67
00:10:52,156 --> 00:10:54,449
'Cause I got a feeling
it's looking at us.

68
00:11:02,625 --> 00:11:04,252
I just want to wake up.

69
00:11:11,258 --> 00:11:14,053
Leaven. We can do this.

70
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:17,848
We just have to stay calm
and work together as a team.

71
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:22,395
There's gonna be a lot of people
looking for us on the outside.

72
00:11:22,978 --> 00:11:23,978
I'm a cop.

73
00:11:24,730 --> 00:11:25,730
All right?

74
00:11:27,191 --> 00:11:28,776
- You're a cop?
- Yeah.

75
00:11:29,902 --> 00:11:32,071
I'm gonna get you out of here.
I promise.

76
00:11:32,947 --> 00:11:34,699
You gotta be with me on this one.

77
00:11:39,954 --> 00:11:40,954
Okay.

78
00:11:52,633 --> 00:11:53,676
Boot it!

79
00:12:01,684 --> 00:12:02,684
Clean.

80
00:12:22,497 --> 00:12:23,998
That one sounded closer.

81
00:12:24,582 --> 00:12:27,210
It's mechanical. It seems
to come at regular intervals.

82
00:12:27,585 --> 00:12:29,462
Maybe it's the ventilation system.

83
00:12:29,670 --> 00:12:32,340
- No vents.
- No kidding, I'm boiling.

84
00:12:35,968 --> 00:12:36,968
What is it?

85
00:12:40,347 --> 00:12:41,473
Serial numbers?

86
00:12:41,807 --> 00:12:44,560
Room numbers.
They're different in each room.

87
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:49,148
Oh great. There are only 566 millions
400 thousand rooms in this thing.

88
00:12:49,231 --> 00:12:50,565
Well, there better not be?

89
00:12:50,650 --> 00:12:52,777
We have about 3 days
without food and water

90
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:54,862
before we are too weak to move.

91
00:12:55,195 --> 00:12:56,906
Well, they have to feed us,
don't they?

92
00:12:58,323 --> 00:12:59,408
Holloway.

93
00:12:59,492 --> 00:13:04,622
Oh, we have heat, stress, physical
exsection, i.e., dehydratation,

94
00:13:04,705 --> 00:13:08,083
headaches, dizziness, disorientation,
confused mental processes.

95
00:13:08,167 --> 00:13:11,086
The body eventually begins
to break down its own tissue.

96
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,214
Suck on it.

97
00:13:18,052 --> 00:13:19,929
Keeps the saliva flowing.

98
00:13:38,405 --> 00:13:40,657
- What?
- The air seems dry in there.

99
00:13:40,991 --> 00:13:41,991
Trapped?

100
00:13:42,242 --> 00:13:44,119
Molecular chemical sensor.

101
00:13:44,286 --> 00:13:46,288
Why the hell didn't
the boot set it off?

102
00:13:46,497 --> 00:13:47,707
The boot's not alive.

103
00:13:48,332 --> 00:13:51,251
Detects hydrogen sulphide
excreted from the skin.

104
00:13:51,711 --> 00:13:53,921
How is it you know
so much about sensors, Renz?

105
00:13:59,176 --> 00:14:03,638
Renn. Not Renz. It's French.

106
00:14:03,848 --> 00:14:05,891
Fine, you're French.
I'm asking how you...

107
00:14:08,978 --> 00:14:11,981
Renn. Sensor expert,

108
00:14:12,064 --> 00:14:13,232
about the right age.

109
00:14:14,108 --> 00:14:15,359
I don't believe it.

110
00:14:19,071 --> 00:14:21,616
- This guy is the Wren.
- The what?

111
00:14:21,949 --> 00:14:26,036
He's the Wren. The Bird of Attica.
Flew the coop on 6 major prisons.

112
00:14:26,537 --> 00:14:27,538
Seven.

113
00:14:27,705 --> 00:14:29,499
You're kidding, right?

114
00:14:30,415 --> 00:14:31,666
You can get us out.

115
00:14:31,876 --> 00:14:32,877
Maybe.

116
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:35,087
An escape artist.

117
00:14:35,170 --> 00:14:37,089
Yeah, I'm Harry fucking Houdini.

118
00:14:39,383 --> 00:14:42,023
The only reason I dragged you
this far is 'cause I need your boots.

119
00:14:42,678 --> 00:14:45,180
If you don't smarten up,
I'll be gone like that.

120
00:14:46,557 --> 00:14:47,850
No more talking.

121
00:14:49,059 --> 00:14:50,352
No more guessing.

122
00:14:51,311 --> 00:14:54,606
Don't even think about nothing
that's not right in front of you.

123
00:14:55,315 --> 00:14:57,192
That's the real challenge.

124
00:14:58,569 --> 00:15:01,156
You got to save yourselves
from yourselves.

125
00:15:11,123 --> 00:15:12,123
Merde.

126
00:15:22,009 --> 00:15:23,343
Get him out!

127
00:15:58,045 --> 00:15:59,296
Oh my god!

128
00:16:07,512 --> 00:16:12,351
So, it was electro chemical or
whatever, right? And he missed it.

129
00:16:13,143 --> 00:16:16,689
The Wren. That's great!
That's fuckin' great!

130
00:16:29,243 --> 00:16:32,872
All right. It's time
to reassess this place.

131
00:16:33,122 --> 00:16:35,457
I've been over it again and again.

132
00:16:35,582 --> 00:16:37,667
Why would they throw
innocent people in here?

133
00:16:37,752 --> 00:16:39,211
Are we being punished?

134
00:16:40,129 --> 00:16:42,631
I've never done anything
to deserve this.

135
00:16:43,090 --> 00:16:44,299
Forget about all that!

136
00:16:45,592 --> 00:16:48,345
You can't see the big picture
from in here, so don't try.

137
00:16:48,595 --> 00:16:50,222
Keep your head down.
Keep it simple.

138
00:16:50,389 --> 00:16:52,557
Just look at what's in front of you.

139
00:16:52,642 --> 00:16:53,768
That's what he said.

140
00:16:54,393 --> 00:16:58,522
Start with us.
We got an escape artist and a cop.

141
00:16:58,773 --> 00:17:00,173
There's gotta be a reason for that.

142
00:17:00,691 --> 00:17:04,570
You're doctor, Holloway. It gives you
a function, a reason, right?

143
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:06,864
No. It's just makes me go why me

144
00:17:06,947 --> 00:17:09,992
and why not one of the other
10 million doctors out there.

145
00:17:16,749 --> 00:17:18,584
Leaven, what are you?

146
00:17:18,959 --> 00:17:25,215
Nothing. I just go to school.
I hang out with my friends.

147
00:17:25,299 --> 00:17:27,801
- What else?
- There's nothing else.

148
00:17:28,844 --> 00:17:32,640
My parents are these people.
I live with them. I'm boring.

149
00:17:33,015 --> 00:17:36,769
I think we have to ask
the big questions.

150
00:17:36,936 --> 00:17:38,270
What does it want?

151
00:17:38,437 --> 00:17:40,105
What is it thinking?

152
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:42,525
One down, four to go.

153
00:17:47,362 --> 00:17:49,573
Why don't you tell us
what your purpose is, Worth?

154
00:17:49,824 --> 00:17:51,367
Often wondered that myself.

155
00:17:57,206 --> 00:17:58,457
I'm just a guy.

156
00:17:58,874 --> 00:18:01,877
I work in an office building,
doing office building stuff.

157
00:18:02,419 --> 00:18:07,132
I wasn't exactly bursting with
"joie de vivre" before I got here.

158
00:18:07,216 --> 00:18:08,843
Life just sucks in general.

159
00:18:09,009 --> 00:18:12,346
- I can't stand that attitude.
- Because he's right.

160
00:18:13,138 --> 00:18:15,349
What's your purpose, Quentin?

161
00:18:20,395 --> 00:18:22,940
Kids, three of them.

162
00:18:24,524 --> 00:18:25,984
I haven't made my peace yet.

163
00:18:28,028 --> 00:18:30,030
I'm getting out of here,
no matter what.

164
00:18:30,197 --> 00:18:32,157
That's where
my strength comes from.

165
00:18:32,825 --> 00:18:34,744
You, people,
find yours wherever you got it.

166
00:18:36,203 --> 00:18:38,163
For Christ's sake, Worth.
What do you live for?

167
00:18:38,247 --> 00:18:40,499
Don't you have a wife or
a girlfriend, or something?

168
00:18:40,708 --> 00:18:43,002
No. I've got a pretty fine
collection of pornography.

169
00:18:43,585 --> 00:18:45,795
Oh, nice, nice.

170
00:18:47,589 --> 00:18:51,218
I haven't got anybody either, but
I'm not giving up! I am pissed off.

171
00:18:51,510 --> 00:18:52,886
They came into our homes!

172
00:18:53,220 --> 00:18:57,474
They stripped us bare.
They took my rings, they took...

173
00:18:58,350 --> 00:19:00,394
...oh, my amethyst.

174
00:19:04,231 --> 00:19:05,983
I wanna know who's responsible.

175
00:19:07,067 --> 00:19:09,569
Leaven. Your glasses?

176
00:19:11,906 --> 00:19:12,948
You don't need them?

177
00:19:13,908 --> 00:19:15,034
They're for reading.

178
00:19:17,619 --> 00:19:21,748
Well they took off our jewelry,
but why they put these on you.

179
00:19:23,250 --> 00:19:24,376
If nothing is random,

180
00:19:25,419 --> 00:19:26,503
why are they here?

181
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:38,182
Leaven. What do you do
in school? Math?

182
00:19:43,437 --> 00:19:44,646
What can they mean?

183
00:19:55,449 --> 00:19:56,741
149.

184
00:20:12,674 --> 00:20:16,386
Prime numbers. I can't believe
I didn't see it before.

185
00:20:16,636 --> 00:20:17,636
See what?

186
00:20:17,762 --> 00:20:20,307
It seems like, if any
of these numbers are prime,

187
00:20:20,432 --> 00:20:21,475
then the room's trapped.

188
00:20:25,104 --> 00:20:28,983
645, 645... That's not prime.

189
00:20:29,774 --> 00:20:32,276
372... no.

190
00:20:33,778 --> 00:20:36,030
649...

191
00:20:37,116 --> 00:20:39,618
Well, 11 times 59.
It's not prime either.

192
00:20:42,079 --> 00:20:43,580
So that room is safe.

193
00:20:44,164 --> 00:20:45,040
Wait.

194
00:20:45,124 --> 00:20:48,377
How can you make that assumption
based on one prime number trap?

195
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:52,631
I'm not. The incinerator thing
was prime 083.

196
00:20:53,298 --> 00:20:56,801
The molecular chemical thing had
137. The acid room had 149.

197
00:20:56,969 --> 00:20:58,369
You remember all that in your head?

198
00:20:58,470 --> 00:20:59,804
I have a facility for it.

199
00:21:00,639 --> 00:21:05,352
Leaven, you beautiful brain.

200
00:21:06,937 --> 00:21:07,937
Boot it.

201
00:21:12,026 --> 00:21:13,318
Okay, out of the way.

202
00:21:13,652 --> 00:21:15,069
Brains before beauty.

203
00:21:21,493 --> 00:21:23,870
Safe, safe.

204
00:21:25,830 --> 00:21:29,250
Prime numbers! Prime numbers!

205
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:40,512
Oh, how long have we been in here?

206
00:21:42,764 --> 00:21:44,015
Nine or ten hours.

207
00:21:46,643 --> 00:21:47,643
How do you know?

208
00:21:49,354 --> 00:21:53,733
Five o'clock shadow. Last thing
I remember was shaving.

209
00:21:55,527 --> 00:21:58,363
I guess
I missed breakfast or lunch...

210
00:21:59,031 --> 00:22:00,199
or whatever.

211
00:22:02,617 --> 00:22:05,287
Don't worry.
I'll be home in time for dinner.

212
00:22:08,248 --> 00:22:10,542
If we get out, I'll make you dinner.

213
00:22:12,669 --> 00:22:13,920
You got a date.

214
00:22:32,939 --> 00:22:33,940
Doin' good.

215
00:22:48,705 --> 00:22:52,166
I need to smoke.
I'd smoke a butt off a sidewalk.

216
00:22:52,834 --> 00:22:56,170
Holloway.
Just reel yourself in a bit. Come on.

217
00:22:56,463 --> 00:22:58,132
We're moving along.
Things are looking up.

218
00:22:58,298 --> 00:23:01,468
Ok, ok. You are right.
I quit smoking years ago.

219
00:23:03,303 --> 00:23:04,638
I just need to be occupied.

220
00:23:05,014 --> 00:23:08,392
Talk then. Have a conversation.
What kind of doctor are you anyway?

221
00:23:09,059 --> 00:23:10,811
Oh, you know, the free kind.

222
00:23:15,107 --> 00:23:17,609
Come on. Help me.
Tell me about your rug rats.

223
00:23:19,111 --> 00:23:23,115
We have three boys. 9, 7 and 5.

224
00:23:23,698 --> 00:23:27,536
Good God. Poor woman.
There's no way I'd survive that.

225
00:23:29,413 --> 00:23:30,539
She didn't either.

226
00:23:33,208 --> 00:23:35,502
She's not dead,
we're just separated.

227
00:23:37,504 --> 00:23:40,465
I'm sorry.
I can't just shoot the breeze.

228
00:23:42,426 --> 00:23:43,843
These numbers aren't prime.

229
00:23:43,927 --> 00:23:45,679
Okay, clear.

230
00:23:50,392 --> 00:23:51,726
Excuse me, sorry.

231
00:23:57,524 --> 00:24:00,360
You, could try and
help me out here, buddy.

232
00:24:00,860 --> 00:24:01,945
No, I couldn't.

233
00:24:11,413 --> 00:24:13,082
This one's trapped too.

234
00:24:19,129 --> 00:24:20,673
We have to backtrack?

235
00:24:24,343 --> 00:24:25,427
Not yet.

236
00:24:32,226 --> 00:24:33,268
Read them to me.

237
00:24:47,116 --> 00:24:50,285
- What are you, his coat rack?
- Oh, please!

238
00:25:01,796 --> 00:25:02,839
It's stuck.

239
00:25:05,842 --> 00:25:06,842
Look out.

240
00:25:14,684 --> 00:25:16,144
This room is green.

241
00:25:21,733 --> 00:25:22,817
Holloway?

242
00:25:30,950 --> 00:25:31,950
Hi there.

243
00:25:36,456 --> 00:25:38,125
This room is green.

244
00:25:38,833 --> 00:25:39,833
Yes, it is.

245
00:25:42,045 --> 00:25:43,963
I wanna go back to the blue room.

246
00:25:45,674 --> 00:25:46,966
What is it? Shock or what?

247
00:25:47,592 --> 00:25:49,303
I think he's mentally handicapped.

248
00:25:50,136 --> 00:25:51,512
I like the blue room.

249
00:25:52,931 --> 00:25:56,392
- Jesus Christ.
- He almost broke my neck.

250
00:25:57,143 --> 00:26:01,022
Hey there, are you all alone?
You want to hold my hand, honey?

251
00:26:02,023 --> 00:26:05,443
Butter first, then honey, Kazan.
Butter first, then honey...

252
00:26:05,610 --> 00:26:09,823
- How'd he survive?
- I want to go back to the blue room.

253
00:26:10,199 --> 00:26:12,910
There's lots of blue rooms.
We'll find you another real soon.

254
00:26:14,328 --> 00:26:15,704
This is just way too bizarre.

255
00:26:16,705 --> 00:26:18,915
Well, you just worry
about your numbers then.

256
00:26:21,501 --> 00:26:23,128
Go on. I'll look after him.

257
00:26:27,090 --> 00:26:30,509
Safe. Obviously,
since he almost fell on my head.

258
00:26:30,802 --> 00:26:33,972
Should we go for a walk, Kazan?

259
00:26:35,014 --> 00:26:36,182
You want to go for a walk?

260
00:26:50,614 --> 00:26:52,866
Let's not make him do
the climbing thing right away.

261
00:26:53,074 --> 00:26:54,074
Holloway...

262
00:26:55,076 --> 00:26:56,119
Hol-lo-way.

263
00:27:01,291 --> 00:27:03,710
Could they have taken us
all the way to New Mexico?

264
00:27:03,835 --> 00:27:05,294
What are you
talking about, Holloway?

265
00:27:06,755 --> 00:27:09,299
I'm talking about where do you
hide something this big.

266
00:27:10,008 --> 00:27:11,593
At least he's good for something.

267
00:27:15,847 --> 00:27:17,607
I'm sorry to shake
your foundations, Quentin,

268
00:27:17,641 --> 00:27:20,018
but you have no idea
where your tax dollars go.

269
00:27:20,727 --> 00:27:22,396
Free clinic doctors?

270
00:27:23,104 --> 00:27:25,481
Only the military
industrial complex could afford

271
00:27:25,565 --> 00:27:27,276
to build something this size.

272
00:27:27,401 --> 00:27:31,030
Holloway, what is
the military industrial complex?

273
00:27:31,112 --> 00:27:32,488
Have you ever been there?

274
00:27:32,572 --> 00:27:34,116
I'm telling you,
it's not that complex.

275
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:35,950
How would you know
from where you are?

276
00:27:37,035 --> 00:27:39,120
Who do you think
the establishment is?

277
00:27:39,203 --> 00:27:40,496
It's just guys like me.

278
00:27:40,872 --> 00:27:43,124
Their desks are bigger,
but their jobs are't.

279
00:27:43,207 --> 00:27:45,168
They don't conspire...
they buy boats.

280
00:27:45,919 --> 00:27:48,880
No, this place is...
remember Scaramanga?

281
00:27:49,756 --> 00:27:51,758
The bad guy in
"The Man With The Golden Gun".

282
00:27:54,093 --> 00:27:56,387
It's some rich
psycho's entertainment.

283
00:27:59,433 --> 00:28:00,600
Is that what you think?

284
00:28:01,685 --> 00:28:02,685
Clear.

285
00:28:13,530 --> 00:28:15,532
Ok. You are a cop.

286
00:28:16,700 --> 00:28:19,703
Single bullet theory. Right on.

287
00:28:30,129 --> 00:28:32,799
- Gas!
- Holloway, get back here!

288
00:28:37,637 --> 00:28:41,057
It's okay.
I just swallowed my button.

289
00:28:45,937 --> 00:28:47,481
I hate this. I hate this.

290
00:28:52,527 --> 00:28:54,738
Your boy is having
a conniption fit in there.

291
00:28:59,242 --> 00:29:01,327
It's like cramming without coffee.

292
00:29:01,661 --> 00:29:03,538
- She needs a break.
- She can do it.

293
00:29:13,507 --> 00:29:14,883
They don't look like prime to me.

294
00:29:15,384 --> 00:29:17,636
Is that your two bits worth, Worth?

295
00:29:18,637 --> 00:29:20,138
For what it's worth.

296
00:29:25,519 --> 00:29:30,732
- Well?
- Well, he's right. Not prime.

297
00:29:35,404 --> 00:29:38,240
Stop! In front of you!

298
00:29:51,961 --> 00:29:52,961
What is it?

299
00:30:03,097 --> 00:30:04,223
Shut up!

300
00:30:07,811 --> 00:30:10,313
I don't know what happened.
It wasn't prime.

301
00:30:12,691 --> 00:30:14,318
Quentin, hold still.

302
00:30:17,195 --> 00:30:21,490
- Somebody stops that racket.
- Worth!

303
00:30:24,619 --> 00:30:25,870
Leave the boots.

304
00:30:35,630 --> 00:30:37,549
And shut the fucking door!

305
00:30:41,595 --> 00:30:43,763
I had a feeling
about that fucking guy.

306
00:30:44,556 --> 00:30:46,100
He knew about that trap.

307
00:30:46,641 --> 00:30:47,976
These numbers aren't prime.

308
00:30:48,059 --> 00:30:49,859
Then your number system failed,
but he knew...

309
00:30:49,978 --> 00:30:51,646
Knew what? How would he know?

310
00:30:51,771 --> 00:30:53,371
You are the paranoid one,
think about it.

311
00:30:53,439 --> 00:30:56,025
His only function so far has been
to kick us when we're down.

312
00:30:56,109 --> 00:30:59,028
So he has a bad attitude. Are you
saying, that makes him a spy?

313
00:30:59,195 --> 00:31:01,823
Trust me on this. It's my job
to read people like an X-Ray.

314
00:31:07,411 --> 00:31:08,704
He doesn't like red rooms.

315
00:31:17,338 --> 00:31:18,381
So what happened?

316
00:31:19,340 --> 00:31:21,467
- You saw what happened.
- Quentin!

317
00:31:21,885 --> 00:31:24,085
I guess the numbers are
more complicated that I thought.

318
00:31:24,262 --> 00:31:25,502
Maybe they mean nothing at all.

319
00:31:25,764 --> 00:31:27,516
No. It means
they are more involved.

320
00:31:28,016 --> 00:31:29,785
They've worked for us up 'till now,
haven't they?

321
00:31:29,809 --> 00:31:31,520
I just need more time with them.

322
00:31:31,811 --> 00:31:34,063
Well, we need to rest anyway.

323
00:31:34,856 --> 00:31:38,109
Well. That's handy. 'Cause there's
not a fuck of a lot else we can do.

324
00:31:51,247 --> 00:31:53,166
Are they telling you anything?

325
00:31:54,292 --> 00:31:55,709
They're not tarot cards.

326
00:31:58,004 --> 00:32:00,757
Do you have any idea how many
variables I have to consider

327
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:03,468
before I can
decipher numbers this size?

328
00:32:04,302 --> 00:32:06,220
They don't reveal
themselves right away.

329
00:32:07,471 --> 00:32:08,597
They're like people.

330
00:32:15,313 --> 00:32:17,065
Oh, gross.

331
00:32:20,359 --> 00:32:23,321
Oh, not here honey.
Over in the corner.

332
00:32:30,494 --> 00:32:32,205
Well, he's just peeing.

333
00:32:33,289 --> 00:32:34,790
Jesus Christ.

334
00:32:35,584 --> 00:32:38,378
That's excellent.
Now it totally reeks in here!

335
00:32:40,797 --> 00:32:42,549
You find this all
pretty funny, don't you?

336
00:32:48,179 --> 00:32:50,098
What's your
fucking problem, Worth?

337
00:32:51,808 --> 00:32:53,768
Even Holloway's
holding up better than you.

338
00:32:54,477 --> 00:32:58,564
Get over there and help her with him.
That's your job. Babysitter.

339
00:33:00,900 --> 00:33:02,444
Jawohl, Kommandant.

340
00:33:05,404 --> 00:33:07,740
Somebody has to take
responsability around here.

341
00:33:08,366 --> 00:33:10,493
And that somebody has to be you.

342
00:33:10,744 --> 00:33:12,704
Not all of us have
the luxury of playing nihilist.

343
00:33:13,121 --> 00:33:15,957
Not all of us are
conceited enough to play hero.

344
00:33:17,959 --> 00:33:19,711
This is a will to live.

345
00:33:19,919 --> 00:33:21,546
Everybody's got it,
Worth, even you.

346
00:33:21,671 --> 00:33:24,007
Especially you,
hiding behind that cynical front.

347
00:33:24,548 --> 00:33:25,549
A will to live.

348
00:33:26,009 --> 00:33:28,595
That's the warm,
cosy feeling deep inside.

349
00:33:29,137 --> 00:33:31,097
Thanks Quentin, I'm a new man.

350
00:33:31,347 --> 00:33:34,808
Oh, poor Worth. Nobody loves me.

351
00:33:35,268 --> 00:33:36,828
If that's the chip
on your shoulder, why

352
00:33:36,853 --> 00:33:37,973
did you lug it all this way?

353
00:33:38,229 --> 00:33:39,814
Why didn't you
just lie down and die?

354
00:33:53,870 --> 00:33:54,871
Do it.

355
00:33:55,413 --> 00:33:58,166
Show us you have some backbone
and jump in the sushi machine.

356
00:33:58,541 --> 00:33:59,667
Be a man.

357
00:34:09,260 --> 00:34:10,428
Thought so.

358
00:34:13,222 --> 00:34:14,682
Fuck you Quentin!

359
00:34:17,310 --> 00:34:19,770
I don't wanna die.
I'm just being realistic.

360
00:34:19,854 --> 00:34:21,749
Do you think they'd go to all
the trouble to build this thing

361
00:34:21,773 --> 00:34:22,857
if we could just walk out?

362
00:34:22,982 --> 00:34:24,209
Do you think
they would have left us clues

363
00:34:24,233 --> 00:34:26,277
and let us beat it so far
if there wasn't a way out?

364
00:34:26,360 --> 00:34:27,611
You think we matter? We don't.

365
00:34:27,737 --> 00:34:30,417
Put us out of your misery so we can
get on with getting out of here.

366
00:34:30,489 --> 00:34:31,865
You're not getting out of here!

367
00:34:31,950 --> 00:34:33,493
- Yes, we are!
- No, you're not!

368
00:34:33,576 --> 00:34:36,662
- Yes, we are!
- There is no way out of here!

369
00:34:52,261 --> 00:34:53,471
Gotchya.

370
00:34:59,728 --> 00:35:03,523
How do you know that?

371
00:35:06,109 --> 00:35:07,610
Answer the question, Worth.

372
00:35:09,612 --> 00:35:11,864
Oh, god.

373
00:35:16,745 --> 00:35:17,912
Who are you?

374
00:35:29,298 --> 00:35:30,758
I'm the poison.

375
00:35:33,302 --> 00:35:34,846
I designed the outer shell.

376
00:35:35,764 --> 00:35:36,848
The what?

377
00:35:38,016 --> 00:35:39,934
The shell. The sarcophagus.

378
00:35:41,269 --> 00:35:42,770
You built this thing?

379
00:35:42,854 --> 00:35:44,147
Not this part. The exterior.

380
00:35:44,272 --> 00:35:47,025
I don't know anything about the
numbers or anything else in here.

381
00:35:48,026 --> 00:35:51,696
I was contracted to draw
plans for a hollow shell.

382
00:35:53,197 --> 00:35:54,323
A cube.

383
00:35:55,199 --> 00:35:58,077
A cube? Why didn't you tell us?

384
00:35:59,162 --> 00:36:02,206
For God's sake, Worth,
you knew what it was.

385
00:36:04,125 --> 00:36:05,293
No.

386
00:36:06,210 --> 00:36:09,047
Worth. You're lying.

387
00:36:13,092 --> 00:36:14,510
Was not at first.

388
00:36:15,386 --> 00:36:16,679
Who's behind it?

389
00:36:20,724 --> 00:36:21,725
I don't know.

390
00:36:22,435 --> 00:36:23,811
Who hired you?

391
00:36:25,771 --> 00:36:26,814
I didn't ask.

392
00:36:29,192 --> 00:36:30,860
I never even left my office.

393
00:36:31,652 --> 00:36:33,987
I talked on the phone to some
people, other guys like me.

394
00:36:34,155 --> 00:36:36,240
Specialists,
working on small details.

395
00:36:36,407 --> 00:36:37,700
Nobody knew what it was.

396
00:36:38,409 --> 00:36:39,535
Nobody cared.

397
00:36:39,743 --> 00:36:42,455
Bullshit.
You knew from square one.

398
00:36:43,331 --> 00:36:46,417
Look at him. He is up
to his eyeballs in this thing.

399
00:36:46,542 --> 00:36:49,795
No, Quentin.
That's how they stay hidden.

400
00:36:50,338 --> 00:36:51,464
You keep everyone separated

401
00:36:51,547 --> 00:36:54,007
so the left hand doesn't know
what the right hand is doing.

402
00:36:54,133 --> 00:36:56,302
The brain
never comes out in the open.

403
00:36:57,261 --> 00:36:58,346
Whose brain?

404
00:36:59,889 --> 00:37:02,141
It's all the same machine, right!

405
00:37:02,266 --> 00:37:06,062
The Pentagone, multinational
corporations, the police.

406
00:37:06,687 --> 00:37:10,524
If you do one little job,
you build a widget in Saskatoon,

407
00:37:10,649 --> 00:37:13,026
and the next thing you know
it's two miles under

408
00:37:13,152 --> 00:37:16,322
the desert, the essential
component of a death machine.

409
00:37:17,031 --> 00:37:19,951
I was right.
All along, my whole life,

410
00:37:20,076 --> 00:37:22,370
I knew it. I told you, Quentin.

411
00:37:22,495 --> 00:37:24,955
Nobody's every gonna
call me paranoid again.

412
00:37:25,123 --> 00:37:28,042
We gotta get out of here and
blow the lid of this thing!

413
00:37:34,423 --> 00:37:36,509
Holloway, you don't get it.

414
00:37:37,343 --> 00:37:39,762
Then help me,
please, I need to know.

415
00:37:41,222 --> 00:37:42,932
This may be hard
for you to understand,

416
00:37:43,057 --> 00:37:44,768
but there's no conspiracy.

417
00:37:45,268 --> 00:37:46,685
Nobody is in charge.

418
00:37:47,270 --> 00:37:51,732
It's a headless blunder operating
under the illusion of a master plan.

419
00:37:52,108 --> 00:37:53,192
Can you grasp that?

420
00:37:53,692 --> 00:37:55,736
Big brother is not watching you.

421
00:37:58,239 --> 00:38:00,199
What kind of
fuckin' explanation is that?

422
00:38:00,366 --> 00:38:01,646
It's the best you are gonna get.

423
00:38:01,700 --> 00:38:03,678
I looked, and the only conclusion
I could come to is that

424
00:38:03,702 --> 00:38:05,078
there is nobody up there.

425
00:38:05,246 --> 00:38:07,373
Somebody had to say
yes to this thing.

426
00:38:07,456 --> 00:38:09,333
What thing?
Only we know what it is.

427
00:38:09,458 --> 00:38:12,545
- We have no idea what it is.
- We know more than anybody else.

428
00:38:13,004 --> 00:38:15,107
I mean, somebody might have
known sometime before they go,

429
00:38:15,131 --> 00:38:17,633
they got fired, or
voted out, or sold it,

430
00:38:18,051 --> 00:38:19,678
but if this place
ever had a purpose,

431
00:38:19,760 --> 00:38:22,220
and it got miscommunicated,
or lost in a shuffle.

432
00:38:22,596 --> 00:38:23,931
I mean, this is and accident,

433
00:38:24,015 --> 00:38:27,435
a forgotten perpetual
public works project.

434
00:38:27,685 --> 00:38:29,405
Do you think anybody
wants to ask questions?

435
00:38:29,603 --> 00:38:31,730
All they want is
a clear conscience,

436
00:38:31,855 --> 00:38:33,106
and a fat paycheck.

437
00:38:33,482 --> 00:38:35,242
I leaned on my shovel
for months on this one.

438
00:38:35,318 --> 00:38:36,694
This was a great job!

439
00:38:39,113 --> 00:38:40,657
Why put people in it?

440
00:38:41,699 --> 00:38:45,744
Because it's here. You have
to use it or you admit it's pointless.

441
00:38:45,869 --> 00:38:48,038
But it is pointless.

442
00:38:49,748 --> 00:38:51,709
Quentin. That's my point.

443
00:38:53,169 --> 00:38:54,879
What have we come to?

444
00:38:56,422 --> 00:38:58,591
It's so much worse than I thought.

445
00:38:59,800 --> 00:39:02,636
Not really. Just more pathetic.

446
00:39:03,596 --> 00:39:05,723
You make me sick, Worth.

447
00:39:06,140 --> 00:39:07,851
I make me sick too.

448
00:39:08,726 --> 00:39:10,227
We're both part of the system.

449
00:39:10,811 --> 00:39:14,314
I drew a box, you walk a beat.
It's like you said, Quentin,

450
00:39:14,440 --> 00:39:16,317
is keep your head down,
keep it simple,

451
00:39:16,442 --> 00:39:17,882
just look at what's in front of you.

452
00:39:17,986 --> 00:39:19,779
I mean, nobody wants to see
the big picture.

453
00:39:20,029 --> 00:39:21,322
Life's too complicated.

454
00:39:22,115 --> 00:39:27,161
I mean, let's face it, the reason
we're here is that it's out of control.

455
00:39:39,757 --> 00:39:41,759
This is how we ruin the world?

456
00:39:42,468 --> 00:39:46,847
Well, have you been on glue
all your lives?

457
00:39:47,473 --> 00:39:51,019
I've felt guilty for ruining
the world since I was like 7.

458
00:39:52,061 --> 00:39:55,690
God, if you need someone
to blame, throw a rock.

459
00:40:02,946 --> 00:40:04,114
Well, I feel better.

460
00:40:05,491 --> 00:40:07,118
That's why you stayed with us.

461
00:40:08,536 --> 00:40:09,828
To confess.

462
00:40:24,510 --> 00:40:27,138
You still looking
for someone to bust, Quentin?

463
00:40:37,231 --> 00:40:39,233
Quentin! Stop it! Stop it!

464
00:40:41,026 --> 00:40:42,235
We need him.

465
00:40:44,780 --> 00:40:45,781
What for?

466
00:40:46,031 --> 00:40:47,991
Have you gone absolutely mad?

467
00:40:48,117 --> 00:40:50,536
He's the only one who knows
anything about the place.

468
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:05,843
- Worth.
- Hi.

469
00:41:06,635 --> 00:41:09,597
- So there's this outer shell.
- Yeah.

470
00:41:09,763 --> 00:41:13,642
- And it's a cube, right? Like this.
- I assume so.

471
00:41:13,851 --> 00:41:16,562
- Are there any doors?
- There's one door.

472
00:41:16,645 --> 00:41:19,064
- Where?
- Wherever the door guy put it.

473
00:41:19,690 --> 00:41:22,318
Six guesses, and
it's sealed from the outside.

474
00:41:23,319 --> 00:41:26,364
And, what are the dimensions
of the outer shell?

475
00:41:28,407 --> 00:41:30,409
434 square feet.

476
00:41:40,294 --> 00:41:41,337
May I?

477
00:41:41,420 --> 00:41:43,297
Come on, honey, slide over.

478
00:41:49,178 --> 00:41:51,430
14 by 14 by 14.

479
00:41:51,722 --> 00:41:54,808
The inner cube can't be flush
with the shell wall, there's a space.

480
00:41:55,518 --> 00:41:56,518
One cube?

481
00:41:56,810 --> 00:41:58,186
I don't know, it makes sense.

482
00:41:59,605 --> 00:42:05,027
Ok. The biggest the cube
can be then is...

483
00:42:05,736 --> 00:42:09,156
26 rooms high,
26 rooms across, so...

484
00:42:09,615 --> 00:42:11,992
17.576 rooms.

485
00:42:12,535 --> 00:42:16,205
Seventeen thousand, five hundred
and seventy-six rooms?

486
00:42:18,832 --> 00:42:20,292
That makes me queasy.

487
00:42:24,338 --> 00:42:25,423
Descartes!

488
00:42:28,176 --> 00:42:31,429
- Leaven, you are a genius.
- What? What?

489
00:42:32,095 --> 00:42:36,266
Cartesian coordinates. Of course,
coded cartesian coordinates.

490
00:42:36,559 --> 00:42:39,520
They're used in geometry to plot
points on a 3-dimensional graph.

491
00:42:39,937 --> 00:42:41,772
In English, slower.

492
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:45,693
Bonjour?
These numbers are markers,

493
00:42:45,943 --> 00:42:48,862
and grid reference, like latitude
and longitude on a map.

494
00:42:49,197 --> 00:42:51,991
The numbers tell us where
we are inside the cube.

495
00:42:52,115 --> 00:42:53,491
Well, where are we?

496
00:42:57,330 --> 00:42:58,330
It works.

497
00:42:58,456 --> 00:43:02,293
Okay. All I have to do is add
the numbers together.

498
00:43:02,918 --> 00:43:04,712
The X coordinate is 19...

499
00:43:05,338 --> 00:43:09,342
Y is 26 rooms...

500
00:43:10,676 --> 00:43:12,177
So that places us...

501
00:43:15,180 --> 00:43:16,807
...seven rooms from the edge.

502
00:43:17,182 --> 00:43:19,351
All right, let's go.

503
00:43:19,727 --> 00:43:23,606
Just out of curiosity, I mean,
don't hit me again, or anything...

504
00:43:23,731 --> 00:43:24,999
but what are you gonna do
when you get there?

505
00:43:25,023 --> 00:43:26,567
Maybe we can get the door open.

506
00:43:27,985 --> 00:43:31,321
What we need is to do figure out
how to get around the traps.

507
00:43:31,405 --> 00:43:32,656
I'm dealing with that Holloway.

508
00:43:32,740 --> 00:43:34,340
I'm looking for
practical solutions here.

509
00:43:34,658 --> 00:43:36,660
Well, you haven't found any yet.

510
00:43:40,248 --> 00:43:44,794
We cut the risk with the numbers
and the boot. Worth will go in first.

511
00:43:44,877 --> 00:43:47,671
No, he won't Quentin!
We take turns!

512
00:43:48,964 --> 00:43:49,964
Relax.

513
00:43:58,516 --> 00:43:59,642
Room for two in there?

514
00:44:06,023 --> 00:44:07,149
What's the matter?

515
00:44:07,608 --> 00:44:10,986
These coordinates. 14, 27, 14.

516
00:44:11,612 --> 00:44:13,906
- What about 'em?
- They don't make sense.

517
00:44:14,365 --> 00:44:16,367
Assuming the cube is
26 rooms across,

518
00:44:16,492 --> 00:44:18,411
there can't be
a coordinate larger than 26.

519
00:44:18,994 --> 00:44:21,246
If this were right, then
we would be outside of the cube.

520
00:44:24,207 --> 00:44:26,334
No, not outside of the cube.

521
00:44:28,296 --> 00:44:30,048
I guess that means
we're not having dinner.

522
00:44:30,839 --> 00:44:37,179
Trap. Trap. Trap. Trap.

523
00:44:39,432 --> 00:44:40,599
Trap!

524
00:44:48,106 --> 00:44:49,274
Trap!

525
00:44:54,572 --> 00:44:55,781
Sound activated.

526
00:45:12,214 --> 00:45:13,214
Lovely.

527
00:45:14,467 --> 00:45:17,053
How come the sound of the door
opening didn't set it off?

528
00:45:17,636 --> 00:45:19,096
Must be rigged to ignore it.

529
00:45:19,179 --> 00:45:21,890
So that's it. The edge is
surrounded by traps.

530
00:45:22,015 --> 00:45:25,686
Well, I guess we have to backtrack,
and try somewhere else.

531
00:45:25,811 --> 00:45:27,980
Who knows how many detours
we'll have to take.

532
00:45:28,606 --> 00:45:30,358
I say we cross the bitch.

533
00:45:30,733 --> 00:45:32,067
Right!

534
00:45:33,110 --> 00:45:35,237
How many boots do we have left,
Holloway?

535
00:45:39,492 --> 00:45:40,701
Get it off him.

536
00:45:41,702 --> 00:45:43,871
We know how it works.
We just have to be quiet.

537
00:45:44,204 --> 00:45:45,748
That's pretty fucking quiet.

538
00:45:46,081 --> 00:45:49,584
I'm glad you're on side,
Worth, 'cause... you're up.

539
00:45:51,211 --> 00:45:52,379
And he is not coming.

540
00:45:52,880 --> 00:45:54,256
Of course, he is.

541
00:45:54,382 --> 00:45:57,468
- No way.
- We are not leaving him behind.

542
00:45:57,635 --> 00:45:58,719
He's unpredictable.

543
00:45:59,136 --> 00:46:00,739
When we get to the edge,
we can come back for him.

544
00:46:00,763 --> 00:46:02,473
But he'll get somebody killed here.

545
00:46:02,848 --> 00:46:03,849
Am I right?

546
00:46:06,059 --> 00:46:07,227
Shame on you.

547
00:46:08,103 --> 00:46:09,980
Will you look at yourselves?

548
00:46:11,231 --> 00:46:12,775
What have you turned into?

549
00:46:13,191 --> 00:46:17,237
They may have taken our lives away,
but we are still human beings.

550
00:46:18,280 --> 00:46:19,990
That's all we've got left.

551
00:46:22,410 --> 00:46:23,827
We'll come back for him.

552
00:46:25,328 --> 00:46:27,372
That's a lie and you know it.

553
00:46:37,591 --> 00:46:38,592
He'll be quiet.

554
00:49:14,707 --> 00:49:17,293
- What are you doing?
- I'm gonna wait for him.

555
00:49:17,876 --> 00:49:19,712
- No.
- You go out, I'm here.

556
00:49:20,045 --> 00:49:21,088
Okay.

557
00:49:32,725 --> 00:49:33,851
This way.

558
00:51:18,706 --> 00:51:21,417
- You fucking fuck!
- That's enough!

559
00:51:21,499 --> 00:51:24,169
- He is a trap!
- Let him go right now!

560
00:51:24,252 --> 00:51:26,880
The law of the jungle!
He is endangering the pack!

561
00:51:27,047 --> 00:51:29,132
Let him go, you Nazi!

562
00:51:31,468 --> 00:51:32,635
What did you call me?

563
00:51:32,803 --> 00:51:35,556
Quentin, you let
that innocent boy go.

564
00:51:37,640 --> 00:51:39,517
You listen to me, woman.

565
00:51:40,268 --> 00:51:43,355
Everyday I mop up
after your bleeding heart.

566
00:51:43,981 --> 00:51:47,776
The only reason you
even exist is because I keep you.

567
00:51:48,902 --> 00:51:50,153
I know your type,

568
00:51:51,029 --> 00:51:54,366
no kids, no man to fuck you.

569
00:51:54,908 --> 00:51:56,619
So you go around outraged,

570
00:51:56,952 --> 00:51:59,287
sticking your nose up
other people's assholes,

571
00:51:59,371 --> 00:52:00,914
sniffing their business!!!

572
00:52:03,166 --> 00:52:05,085
You missed your boat, Holloway.

573
00:52:08,171 --> 00:52:10,632
You're all dried up
inside there, aren't you?

574
00:52:11,299 --> 00:52:13,010
That's your fucking problem.

575
00:52:13,844 --> 00:52:16,138
How dare you say that to her?

576
00:52:17,264 --> 00:52:20,433
You don't know her, Quentin.
None of us know each other here.

577
00:52:20,558 --> 00:52:24,020
- Oh, I do.
- No you don't.

578
00:52:24,396 --> 00:52:26,814
No wonder your wife left you.

579
00:52:28,650 --> 00:52:31,944
All that bottled up anger.

580
00:52:33,989 --> 00:52:36,241
And a thing for young girls.

581
00:52:46,584 --> 00:52:48,170
God help you, Quentin.

582
00:52:50,172 --> 00:52:52,340
Did you smack
your kids around too?

583
00:53:06,855 --> 00:53:11,527
Is anybody besides me interested in
what's on the other side of that door?

584
00:53:14,696 --> 00:53:15,697
Open it.

585
00:53:23,330 --> 00:53:26,583
Door number six? Not number one?
Door number two?

586
00:53:28,376 --> 00:53:29,877
Open the fuckin' thing.

587
00:53:32,380 --> 00:53:36,093
Oh, sunshine.

588
00:54:01,952 --> 00:54:02,953
Night time.

589
00:54:03,871 --> 00:54:05,664
My old friend, the shell.

590
00:54:08,250 --> 00:54:11,253
It's there. Morning!

591
00:54:14,797 --> 00:54:15,797
Hang on to me.

592
00:54:24,349 --> 00:54:25,517
I can't see shit.

593
00:54:28,020 --> 00:54:29,187
Nothin' to hang on to.

594
00:54:34,609 --> 00:54:35,693
We gotta try something.

595
00:54:36,319 --> 00:54:37,820
We gotta see
if the door's over there.

596
00:54:39,531 --> 00:54:41,451
Someone has to swing
over there, and take a look.

597
00:54:41,699 --> 00:54:42,699
Swing?

598
00:54:44,577 --> 00:54:47,038
We make a rope, out of clothes.

599
00:54:48,248 --> 00:54:49,958
Take 'em off.
I'll tie it around myself.

600
00:54:50,667 --> 00:54:51,918
Ah, yeah, and you're gonna go.

601
00:54:52,169 --> 00:54:54,546
You weight like 500 ponds,
it'll snap in two seconds.

602
00:54:55,505 --> 00:54:56,548
I'm the lightest.

603
00:54:57,340 --> 00:54:58,340
Forget it.

604
00:54:58,841 --> 00:54:59,842
I'll go.

605
00:55:01,136 --> 00:55:02,429
I'm going, Holloway.

606
00:55:03,055 --> 00:55:05,223
She's right Quentin,
you're too heavy.

607
00:55:05,557 --> 00:55:07,225
I'm the lightest after Leaven.

608
00:55:08,101 --> 00:55:09,687
Anyway, it's my turn.

609
00:55:16,234 --> 00:55:19,196
How long did you know
people were being put in here?

610
00:55:20,113 --> 00:55:21,406
A couple of months.

611
00:55:22,157 --> 00:55:23,450
That's not long,

612
00:55:23,908 --> 00:55:25,409
if you consider your whole life.

613
00:55:26,369 --> 00:55:27,369
I am.

614
00:55:28,580 --> 00:55:30,748
You opened my eyes Worht.
That's something.

615
00:55:33,126 --> 00:55:34,126
David.

616
00:55:36,171 --> 00:55:37,171
Helen.

617
00:55:40,383 --> 00:55:41,801
You're such a Helen.

618
00:56:30,100 --> 00:56:31,769
That's as far as you go.

619
00:56:36,398 --> 00:56:37,941
There's nothing down here.

620
00:56:39,859 --> 00:56:40,860
Hold tight.

621
00:56:42,070 --> 00:56:43,614
I try swinging over there.

622
00:56:53,206 --> 00:56:55,000
Brace yourselves,
I'm gonna try again.

623
00:57:01,131 --> 00:57:06,344
- Okay, one more time.
- Hurry, you're getting heavy.

624
00:57:17,730 --> 00:57:19,566
What the hell's going on?

625
00:57:20,067 --> 00:57:21,694
Get up here now!

626
00:57:54,351 --> 00:57:55,894
- Quentin!
- Have you got her?

627
00:57:56,561 --> 00:58:00,440
- What's going on?
- Quentin, is she okay?

628
00:58:26,716 --> 00:58:30,928
She... slipped.

629
00:58:32,430 --> 00:58:33,431
Holloway?

630
00:59:05,255 --> 00:59:06,882
Hey, shhh...
Come on, Kazan.

631
00:59:08,883 --> 00:59:10,843
Kazan, will you please
stop doing that?

632
00:59:11,803 --> 00:59:15,557
Leaven, you got be strong,
sweetheart.

633
00:59:15,682 --> 00:59:17,016
Don't even talk to me.

634
00:59:19,519 --> 00:59:21,104
We gotta get down to the bottom.

635
00:59:23,356 --> 00:59:25,608
It will be easier to get on
to the shell from there.

636
00:59:27,652 --> 00:59:30,154
It's a long fucking way
with only one boot.

637
00:59:30,488 --> 00:59:32,824
But we gotta do it
before we get too weak.

638
00:59:34,409 --> 00:59:36,328
You gotta keep
cracking the numbers, Leaven.

639
00:59:37,662 --> 00:59:39,247
I can't think anymore.

640
00:59:39,372 --> 00:59:42,375
Sure you can. It's your gift.

641
00:59:42,959 --> 00:59:46,045
It's not a gift. It's just a brain.

642
00:59:47,214 --> 00:59:50,258
Let her sleep for a while. We haven't
slept in fuck knows how long.

643
00:59:51,801 --> 00:59:52,969
All right.

644
00:59:54,596 --> 00:59:55,680
One hour.

645
00:59:56,473 --> 00:59:58,850
How the fuck are you gonna know
how long an hour is?

646
01:00:00,685 --> 01:00:03,230
An hour is as long as I say.

647
01:01:08,252 --> 01:01:09,545
What are you doing?

648
01:01:11,756 --> 01:01:13,236
We have to make it down
to the bottom.

649
01:01:13,550 --> 01:01:15,427
It'll be quiet there, and
you can concentrate.

650
01:01:17,094 --> 01:01:19,639
- You just want to leave them?
- They're traps, Leaven.

651
01:01:20,890 --> 01:01:21,974
We are the key.

652
01:01:22,392 --> 01:01:24,852
I'll get us down there.
You think us out.

653
01:01:25,395 --> 01:01:26,438
Believe in me!

654
01:01:26,854 --> 01:01:29,649
Try and see what I see,
how my mind works.

655
01:01:29,774 --> 01:01:32,610
The flash when I look into someone's
head like a fucking X-ray.

656
01:01:36,280 --> 01:01:37,531
I looked through the walls.

657
01:01:38,408 --> 01:01:42,454
I dreamed him at his desk,
designing everything.

658
01:01:45,081 --> 01:01:46,850
He can't let you solve the puzzle,
see, 'cause

659
01:01:46,874 --> 01:01:48,125
there is a purpose.

660
01:01:48,668 --> 01:01:50,127
We are the purpose. The cube...

661
01:01:51,045 --> 01:01:52,088
...is us.

662
01:01:53,840 --> 01:01:56,968
- Quentin.
- We fit. Like numbers.

663
01:01:58,636 --> 01:02:01,556
A man and a woman.
Two halves of the equation.

664
01:02:02,890 --> 01:02:06,478
I take you down, the perfect key.

665
01:02:07,144 --> 01:02:08,520
I slip you in the lock.

666
01:02:13,985 --> 01:02:17,238
Leaven, it's time to go down.

667
01:02:32,086 --> 01:02:33,087
Get away from her.

668
01:02:35,339 --> 01:02:38,050
Leaven, they're fuckin' spies.

669
01:02:38,342 --> 01:02:39,676
Him, the retard.

670
01:02:40,261 --> 01:02:42,889
Holloway, had outside
information about my family...

671
01:02:42,972 --> 01:02:45,892
but she slipped up, didn't she?
She crossed the line!

672
01:02:48,645 --> 01:02:50,272
You dropped her.

673
01:02:54,150 --> 01:02:55,317
Just go, Quentin.

674
01:02:56,861 --> 01:02:59,030
Give us the boot, you pig!

675
01:03:18,174 --> 01:03:19,759
You don't want the boot.

676
01:03:40,697 --> 01:03:44,116
You want to came with us, Worth?
Down the hatch.

677
01:03:52,041 --> 01:03:53,375
What the fuck's with him?

678
01:04:41,591 --> 01:04:42,800
How did...

679
01:04:44,677 --> 01:04:49,599
It's, it's, it's the Wren.
It's the old Wrenster.

680
01:04:51,518 --> 01:04:52,769
How could...

681
01:04:53,686 --> 01:04:56,022
We've been going around in circles.

682
01:04:57,023 --> 01:04:58,065
That can't be.

683
01:05:02,529 --> 01:05:04,614
- Where are we?
- I don't know!

684
01:05:06,616 --> 01:05:08,910
Where are we?

685
01:05:14,373 --> 01:05:15,624
You figure it out!

686
01:05:15,833 --> 01:05:19,504
You haven't done anything.
All you do is freak out you,

687
01:05:20,087 --> 01:05:21,422
murderer!

688
01:06:03,715 --> 01:06:05,342
I guess you were right, Worth.

689
01:06:06,634 --> 01:06:08,345
There is no way out of here.

690
01:06:34,996 --> 01:06:36,497
Get away from me.

691
01:07:11,573 --> 01:07:13,242
Wasn't Rennes killed in that room?

692
01:07:24,378 --> 01:07:25,963
How come there's nothing out there?

693
01:07:28,675 --> 01:07:29,842
It's the edge.

694
01:07:30,051 --> 01:07:32,762
We weren't at the edge before.
Where's the room that killed Rennes?

695
01:07:33,846 --> 01:07:35,056
Fuck off!

696
01:07:39,727 --> 01:07:41,062
Oh, that was good.

697
01:07:41,771 --> 01:07:45,400
What difference does it make?
We're dead anyways.

698
01:07:45,566 --> 01:07:50,112
Hey, listen to what I'm saying.
There was a room there before.

699
01:07:52,448 --> 01:07:55,534
We haven't been moving in circles.
The rooms have.

700
01:07:55,910 --> 01:07:58,412
- Of course.
- The rooms?

701
01:07:58,746 --> 01:08:00,457
That explains
the thunder and the shaking.

702
01:08:00,581 --> 01:08:02,291
We've been shifting the whole time.

703
01:08:04,376 --> 01:08:06,837
It's the only logical explanation.

704
01:08:09,548 --> 01:08:11,258
I'm such an idiot!

705
01:08:12,093 --> 01:08:14,553
- What are you on to, Leaven?
- Give me a minute.

706
01:08:17,348 --> 01:08:19,892
The numbers are markers,
points on a map, right?

707
01:08:20,392 --> 01:08:21,392
Right.

708
01:08:22,478 --> 01:08:25,731
How do you map a point
that keeps moving?

709
01:08:28,943 --> 01:08:30,236
Permutations.

710
01:08:32,739 --> 01:08:33,740
Permu what?

711
01:08:34,866 --> 01:08:35,908
Permutations.

712
01:08:35,992 --> 01:08:38,661
A list of all the coordinates
that the room passes through.

713
01:08:38,745 --> 01:08:40,680
Like a map, that tells you
where the rooms starts,

714
01:08:40,704 --> 01:08:43,081
how many times it moves,
and where it moves to.

715
01:08:44,291 --> 01:08:45,960
The numbers tell you all that?

716
01:08:46,460 --> 01:08:48,087
I don't know,

717
01:08:48,170 --> 01:08:50,107
see, I've only been looking
at one point on the map,

718
01:08:50,131 --> 01:08:52,174
which is probably
the starting position.

719
01:08:52,842 --> 01:08:56,303
All I saw was what the cube looked
like before it started to move.

720
01:08:56,553 --> 01:08:57,888
Okay, so it's moving.

721
01:09:01,308 --> 01:09:02,559
How do we get out?

722
01:09:05,104 --> 01:09:06,397
27.

723
01:09:10,777 --> 01:09:12,529
I know where the exit is.

724
01:09:13,863 --> 01:09:14,863
Where?

725
01:09:15,614 --> 01:09:17,949
- Stay away from me.
- Back off, Quentin.

726
01:09:19,118 --> 01:09:20,411
I just wanna know.

727
01:09:21,662 --> 01:09:22,996
Don't you wanna know?

728
01:09:27,043 --> 01:09:29,253
You remember that room
we passed through before,

729
01:09:29,503 --> 01:09:31,797
the one with the coordinate
larger than 26?

730
01:09:32,256 --> 01:09:33,299
What about it?

731
01:09:34,383 --> 01:09:38,470
That coordinate placed the room
outside the cube.

732
01:09:41,140 --> 01:09:42,140
A bridge.

733
01:09:42,558 --> 01:09:45,977
Right.
But only in its original position.

734
01:09:47,604 --> 01:09:48,897
What are you talking about?

735
01:09:52,776 --> 01:09:55,987
Look.
The room starts off as a bridge,

736
01:09:56,113 --> 01:09:58,115
and then it moves its way
through the maze,

737
01:09:58,240 --> 01:09:59,658
which is where we ran into it.

738
01:10:00,076 --> 01:10:03,120
But at some point,
it must return to its original position.

739
01:10:03,245 --> 01:10:06,248
- So a bridge is only a bridge.
- For a short period of time.

740
01:10:06,707 --> 01:10:09,251
This thing is like
a giant combination lock.

741
01:10:09,376 --> 01:10:11,855
When the rooms are in their
starting position, the lock is open.

742
01:10:11,879 --> 01:10:14,340
But when they move
out of alignment, the lock closes.

743
01:10:14,548 --> 01:10:16,425
With a structure this size,
it must take days

744
01:10:16,550 --> 01:10:18,427
for the rooms
to complete a full cycle.

745
01:10:18,970 --> 01:10:20,346
So, when does it open?

746
01:10:29,897 --> 01:10:30,898
Don't.

747
01:10:31,565 --> 01:10:34,125
To find the original coordinates,
the numbers are added together.

748
01:10:34,151 --> 01:10:36,904
To find the permutations, they're
subtracted from one another.

749
01:10:40,157 --> 01:10:41,157
That's it!

750
01:10:41,951 --> 01:10:45,454
This room moves to zero,
1 and -1 on the X-axis.

751
01:10:45,621 --> 01:10:47,664
2, 5 and -7 on Y.

752
01:10:48,290 --> 01:10:51,127
And 1, and -1 and zero on Z.

753
01:10:51,335 --> 01:10:52,794
And what does that mean?

754
01:10:53,504 --> 01:10:54,755
You suck at math?

755
01:10:55,297 --> 01:10:57,842
Okay, I need the room numbers
around us as reference points.

756
01:11:00,302 --> 01:11:04,223
666, 897, 466.

757
01:11:06,267 --> 01:11:11,022
- 567, 898. Okay?
- Yes.

758
01:11:11,105 --> 01:11:14,275
And 545.
Did you get that?

759
01:11:18,320 --> 01:11:22,574
656, 778, 462.

760
01:11:23,993 --> 01:11:28,247
That's enough.
X is 17, Y is 25 and Z is 14.

761
01:11:31,500 --> 01:11:33,794
Which means
this room makes 2 more moves

762
01:11:33,877 --> 01:11:35,921
before returning
to its original position.

763
01:11:36,005 --> 01:11:37,882
- Do we have time?
- Maybe.

764
01:11:38,007 --> 01:11:39,007
Then let's go!

765
01:11:39,133 --> 01:11:40,610
Can you work
the traps into this system?

766
01:11:40,634 --> 01:11:42,636
Fuck the traps.
Let's get to the bridge.

767
01:11:42,719 --> 01:11:45,180
You threw out our last boot,
you fucking idiot.

768
01:11:45,264 --> 01:11:48,142
- Technically, I can identify the traps.
- Technically?

